-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",109,{
[3457]="70058579\n1\tDefeat Gundabad black-arrows (total: 6)\030Defeat Gundabad warriors (total: 6)\tZarkul-sulûn can be found in southern Elderslade. You should defeat enemies within the ruins of Zarkul-sulûn.\n2\tReturn to Gunvald\tGunvald is in Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade. Return to Gunvald.\n",
[3458]="70032B95\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Mudmul-charâf (total: 10)\tOrcs can be found in Mudmul-charâf, in the north-west passages of Zelem-melek. You should defeat Orcs in Mudmul-charâf.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated several Orcs in their encampment in Mudmul-charâf, making the halls of Zelem-melek safer for travellers to and from the Twenty-first Hall.\n",
[3459]="7005B224\n1\tBurning Orc corpses in Shataz-kordh may cause your next target to leave the nest.\t\n2\tTalk to Elta near Shataz-kordh\tYou have burned all of the Orc corpses in Shataz-kordh. Elta waits for your return outside the worm nest.\n",
[3460]="7004CE2C\n1\tComplete: Trouble Comes Down the Mountain\030Complete: Thievery on the River\030Complete: Victims of the Ambushers\tLorndúr can be found in Loeglond. You should complete quests for Lorndúr.\n2\tTalk to Lorndúr\tLorndúr can be found in Loeglond. You should talk to Lorndúr.\n",
[3461]="7003FF7B\n1\tDisable traps (total: 8)\tThe traps must be removed for the people to safely return.\n",
[3462]="70032BE7\n1\tSpeak with Thithrand in Orc-watch\tThe dwarves of the Orc-watch are fewer in number these days. Long-standing dwellers left in a fellowship seeking riches and adventure in the Redhorn Lodes below.\n2\tSpeak with Ossur in the Orc-watch\tThe dwarves of the Orc-watch are fewer in number these days. Long-standing dwellers left in a fellowship seeking riches and adventure in the Redhorn Lodes below.\n3\tSpeak with Isólf in the Orc-watch\tThe dwarves of the Orc-watch are fewer in number these days. Long-standing dwellers left in a fellowship seeking riches and adventure in the Redhorn Lodes below.\n4\tClean up goat droppings on the road (total: 6)\tThe road from Orc-watch to the Redhorn Lodes is in need of clearing, as quite a mess was left in the wake of the dwarf-fellowship.\n5\tSpeak with Ingifast\tA few members of the dwarf-fellowship have made camp at the bottom of the stairs toward the Redhorn. They chose not to abandon their goat and waggon.\n6\tDrop the 'mess' on the pile near the goat\tThe goat seems to have made a pile of... mess in a corner of the camp. This would be a good place to put the... mess from the road.\n7\tReturn to Ingifast\tThe dwarves of the camp will be more eager to talk to you now that you've rid yourself of the smell. But, first impressions are first impressions, and they may remember you for that.\n",
[3463]="700399FC\n1\tDestroy Avanc-jaw traps (total: 8)\tAvanc-jaw traps can be found along the road west out of Middlemead in Kingstead. You have discovered cruel Dunlending traps and should destroy them to protect the warriors and steeds of Middlemead.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many Avanc-jaw traps and cleared the road for passing Rohirrim.\n",
[3464]="7006EC09\n1\tDiscover attack locations (total: 5)\030Defeat brigands (total: 11)\tYour mission is to investigate the area where there have been many reports of brigands and put a stop to them and their leader, Ulâmul the Talon.\n2\tDefeat Ulâmul the Talon\tUlâmul the Talon has arrived. Defeat him!\n",
[3465]="7000E83B\n1\tDefeat Tarkrîp Orcs in Nan Wathren (total: 15)\tTarkrîp Orcs can be found in Nan Wathren, north-east of Trestlebridge in the North Downs, far to the north of Bree. Nidgyl has asked you to defeat the Tarkrîp Orcs in Nan Wathren.\n2\tTalk to Nidgyl\tNidgyl is at Bree-town in Bree-land, far to the south of the North Downs. You should return to Nidgyl and tell him of your assault against the Tarkrîp Orcs.\n",
[3466]="7002844A\n1\tDefeat half-orc ambushers (total: 10)\tThere are half-orcs along the road to Isengard. Dagoras has asked you to defeat the half-orcs waiting in ambush for Grimbold's emissary.\n2\tTalk to Dagoras near the gates of Isengard\tDagoras is encamped near the gates of Isengard. You should return to Dagoras with news of your success.\n",
[3467]="7004A8FA\n1\tDefeat Lugvarg warriors (total: 6)\030Defeat Lugvarg sentries (total: 6)\tOrkish warriors and sentries can be found at the watch-tower of Lugvarg along the Morgai in Rath Cail. You have come to Lugvarg in search of rumoured belongings of Frodo or Sam, and have found that the watch-tower guards the pass to Magh Ashtu in Dor Amarth. You should defeat many of the Orcs in Lugvarg.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many of the Orcs in Lugvarg.\n",
[3468]="7007161C\n1\tTalk to Captain Hanâbu outside Jolakhúro\tCaptain Hanâbu has gone ahead to attack the Ordâkhai forward camp, Jolakhúro. You should meet up with Captain Hanâbu outside Jolakhúro.\n2\tComplete 'Clearing the Way: Assault on Jolakhúro'\030Complete 'Clearing the Way: Ordâkhai Obstacles'\tCaptain Hanâbu needs your assistance clearing the path for the incoming army. You should complete 'Clearing the Way: Assault on Jolakhúro' and 'Clearing the Way: Ordâkhai Obstacles'.\n3\tTalk to Captain Hanâbu\tYou have done much to clear the path to Emax Dûl. You should talk to Captain Hanâbu outside Jolakhúro.\n4\tMeet Mizâdi at the bridge to Emax Dûl\tMizâdi has gone ahead with her Subuzûri to claim the bridge to Emax Dûl. You should meet Mizâdi just up the road from Jolakhúro.\n",
[3469]="70072B90\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai in Jolakhúro (total: 10)\030Defeat Orihóta Bóro\tThe Ordâkhai camp, Jolakhúro, must be cleared in preparation for the arrival of Mizâdi's allied forces. You should help the Aradûni soldiers defeat the Ordâkhai and their leader, Orihóta Bóro.\n2\tTalk to Captain Hanâbu\tThe Ordâkhai in Jolakhúro have been defeated. You should return to Captain Hanâbu.\n",
[3470]="70072B91\n1\tDestroy Ordâkhai barricades (total: 10)\tThe Ordâkhai have placed barricades along the road to Emax Dûl to slow an advancing army. You should destroy the Ordâkhai barricades.\n2\tTalk to Captain Hanâbu\tThe barricades have been destroyed. You should return to Captain Hanâbu.\n",
[3471]="70048C93\n1\tDefeat Stained merrevail (total: 10)\tStained merrevail can be found near Seregost. You should defeat any Stained merrevail you find.\n2\tCompleted.\t\n",
[3472]="700164CA\n1\tCollect glass-spider legs (total: 10)\tGlass-spiders can be found to the west of the Rotting Cellar, near The Lost Palace. Thrand wishes to repair some of the dwarf-lamps smashed by the goblins and speculates that glass-spider legs will make the best replacements for the crystals.\n2\tTalk to Thrand in the Rotting Cellar\030Collect Glass-spider Leg (total: 10)\tThrand is in the Rotting Cellar, east of The Lost Palace. Thrand will be delighted to see the condition of the glass-spider legs you collected.\n",
[3473]="70030867\n1\tComplete 'Circling The Kill'\030Complete 'Borrowing Barricades'\030Complete 'A Cut Above'\030Complete 'A Controlled Pyre'\030Complete 'Crippling The Front'\tWinsig has directed you to assault the Orc camps to the south-west and west of Walstow.\n2\tTalk to Winsig\tAs you've completely destroyed the Orc fortifications, you should now return to Winsig with news of your victory. Winsig can be found in the mead-hall of Walstow.\n",
[3474]="7003FF21\n1\tDestroy grappling hooks (total: 6)\tThe grappling hooks should be removed so no more corsairs may climb them.\n",
[3475]="7004E4F0\n1\tChallenge and defeat Jáldor\tJáldor can be found somewhere inside Utterby. You should challenge and defeat Jáldor.\n2\tTalk to Kunchat\tKunchat has heard of your victory and wishes to speak with you. You should talk to Kunchat.\n3\t\"Help\" Yólkhon with 'Loosen their Shackles'\030Help Tuhâl with 'Bolstering the Feeble'\030\"Help\" Yólkhon with 'Lest They Fall Victim'\030Help Tuhâl with 'Feeding the Starved'\tKunchat may let you challenge another Jangovar leader as you earn his favour. You should complete more quests in Utterby.\n4\tTalk to Kunchat\tKunchat is ready to give you the name of another Jangovar to challenge. You should talk to Kunchat.\n5\tChallenge and defeat Sháwat\tSháwat can be found somewhere inside Utterby. You should challenge and defeat Sháwat.\n6\tTalk to Kunchat\tKunchat has heard of your victory and wishes to speak with you. You should talk to Kunchat.\n7\t\"Help\" Otkóz with 'Defensive Damage'\030\"Help\" Otkóz with 'Destructive Disarmament'\tKunchat may let you challenge another Jangovar leader as you earn his favour. You should complete more quests in Utterby.\n8\tTalk to Kunchat\tKunchat is ready to give you the name of another Jangovar to challenge. You should talk to Kunchat.\n9\tChallenge and defeat Bakhíl\tBakhíl can be found somewhere inside Utterby. You should challenge and defeat Bakhíl.\n10\tTalk to Kunchat\tKunchat is pleased with your prowess in duels. You should talk to Kunchat.\n",
[3476]="700033D0\n1\tLook for signs of the \"Black Rider\"\tThe \"Black Rider\" was seen in Cam Puddifoot's fields, east of Budgeford. Odovacar Bolger told you that one of his neighbours, Cam Puddifoot, reported the Black Rider on his land, being chased by wolves. Odovacar has asked you to go look for the horseless \"Rider\".\n2\tBring black cloak to Odovacar Bolger\tOdovacar Bolger is at his home up the hill in the centre of Budgeford. Odovacar Bolger sent you to search Puddifoot's fields for signs of the Black Rider, but all you found was a ruined black cloak. You should bring the cloak back to Odovacar.\n",
[3477]="70025134\n1\tTalk to Frithgeir in Zudrugund\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund, which lies within Nár's Peak, north of the river. The eye you recovered will long serve as a symbol of the defeat of the gwiber that menaced Thrór's Coomb.\n",
[3478]="70022A85\n1\tTalk to Frithgeir in Zudrugund\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund, which lies within Nár's Peak, north of the river. The fang you recovered will long serve as a symbol of the defeat of the gwiber that menaced Thrór's Coomb.\n",
[3479]="700032D0\n1\tClose shrew burrows (total: 4)\tThere are shrew burrows to the east of Michel Delving, beyond the Delving Fields. Ruby Primstone is upset by the ruination of the greenery caused by the shrews and wants you to close up some of their burrows.\n2\tTalk to Ruby Primstone\tRuby Primstone is in Michel Delving, at her home south-east of the statue of Marcho and Blanco in the centre of town. Ruby will be pleased to hear that you have closed some of the shrew burrows near the town.\n",
[3480]="7003FF7A\n1\tClose the gate to the port\tThe gate to the port should be closed to seal the corsairs off from their ships.\n",
[3481]="7006944C\n1\tComplete Umbar Tailor's Guild daily orders (total: 5)\tComplete requests from the Umbar Tailor's Guild. You can acquire these quests from the Umbar Tailor's Guild Leader in the Umbar Baharbêl craft guild hall.\n2\tCompleted\tYou completed many Umbar tailor requests.\n",
[3482]="7000178B\n1\tDisable burning idols in Tham Lorn\tBurning idols can be found at Tham Lorn in the western Fields of Fornost. You should disable the idols, and stop the corruption from this part of Fornost.\n2\tDisable burning idols in Tham Lorn (total: 6)\tBurning idols can be found at Tham Lorn in the western Fields of Fornost. You should disable the idols, and stop the corruption from this part of Fornost.\n3\tReturn to Mincham\tMincham awaits you at his camp. You have disabled many of the burning idols at Tham Lorn, and should tell Mincham what you accomplished.\n",
[3483]="7005B49D\n1\tTalk to Nósni\tNósni is located in Hagbuth. Mother Amma has asked you to speak to Nósni.\n2\tSearch for signs of corruption\tClovengap mist-stalkers and sabre-tooth cats can be found in the vineyards in eastern Clovengap. Mother Amma has asked you to look into whether the Angmarim have managed to corrupt the sabre-tooth cats that prowl Maranazhâr.\n3\tContinue searching for signs of corruption\tDeadly sabre-cats prowl the Maranazhâr vineyards in eastern Clovengap. Look for more clues as to whether the Angmarim have managed to corrupt the sabre-tooth cats.\n4\tExamine the waggon\tIn the crumbling vineyards of Maranazhâr, you have discovered an Angmarim waggon. The Angmarim have intentions of creating abominations out of the already fierce sabre-tooth cats! You should defeat the Angmarim!\n5\tSearch for clues\tThe Angmarim experiments were going to take place in the vineyards. With the Angmarim sorceress Iuvár defeated, you should look for clues about their experiments.\n6\tReturn to Mother Amma\tMother Amma is in Hagbuth, in south-eastern Clovengap. You should tell Mother Amma what you found in the vineyards.\n",
[3484]="7005A740\n1\tDefeat Ilvind\030Defeat Muzhudh\tDefeat Ilvind or Muzhudh.\n2\tTalk to Zádokh Flint-eye\tYou should return to Zádokh Flint-eye and apprise him of your efforts.\n",
[3485]="7005A73C\n1\tCollect logs (total: 10)\tCollect logs.\n",
[3486]="7005A739\n1\tDefeat Wargs (total: 15)\030Defeat drakes (total: 15)\tDefeat wargs or drakes.\n",
[3487]="7005297D\n1\tEnter Gálhyrst\tGálhyrst can be found on the southern edge of the Beorning-lands. You should defeat the Huorns and vicious hornets found at Gálhyrst.\n2\tDefeat Huorns at Gálhyrst (total: 4)\030Defeat Clutchroot\030Defeat vicious hornets at Gálhyrst (total: 6)\tGálhyrst can be found on the southern edge of the Beorning-lands. You should defeat the Huorns and vicious hornets found at Gálhyrst.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated Huorns and hornets at Gálhyrst.\n",
[3488]="70033033\n1\tDestroy boxes of coal\tBoxes of coal can be found in the forges of Uzbad-bakân in Zelem-melek. You should destroy boxes of coal to hinder the weapon and armour-crafting of the Orcs of Moria.\n2\tDestroy boxes of coal (total: 5)\tBoxes of coal can be found in the forges of Uzbad-bakân in Zelem-melek. You should destroy boxes of coal to hinder the weapon and armour-crafting of the Orcs of Moria.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed the coal intended to fuel the forges of Uzbad-bakân, hindering the armour and weapon-craft of Moria's Orcs.\n",
})
